{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-74094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $‖v‖=6$ and $u\\cdot v=-9$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-9| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot 6 \\\\ 9 & \\le 6\\cdot ‖u‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le 2\\cdot ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3 & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot ‖u‖ \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & \\le ‖u‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$\nis  $\\frac{3}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-74094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-39430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $‖u‖=3$ and $u\\cdot v=4$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-39430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |4| & \\le 3\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le 3\\cdot ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 4 & \\le \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & \\le ‖v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$\nis  $\\frac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-39430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-39430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-39430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-39430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{k} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u\\cdot v=-20$ and $‖v‖=5$,  what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n|u\\cdot v|\\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $‖u‖.$ So first, we compute $‖u‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-20| & \\le \\sqrt{14+k}\\cdot (5) \\\\ 4 & \\le \\sqrt{14+k} \\\\ {4}^{2} & \\le {(\\sqrt{14+k})}^{2} \\\\ 16 & \\le 14+k \\\\ 2 & \\le k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-40882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{k} \\\\ -\\sqrt{k} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u\\cdot v=-2$ and $‖v‖=1$, what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n|u\\cdot v|\\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $‖u‖.$ So first, we compute $‖u‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+2k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-2| & \\le \\sqrt{2+2k}\\cdot (1) \\\\ 2 & \\le \\sqrt{2+2k} \\\\ {2}^{2} & \\le {(\\sqrt{2+2k})}^{2} \\\\ 4 & \\le 2+2k \\\\ 2 & \\le 2k \\\\ k & \\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-140442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140442" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $‖u‖=5$ and $u\\cdot v=-15$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-15| & \\le 5\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 15 & \\le 5\\cdot ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{5}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 15 & \\le \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$\nis  $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-140440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors  $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(-1)+(2)(-1)+(3)(2)+(-4)(0)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6})≈{68.12}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-40561" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40561" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{15.25}^{∘}"] ["math" "{33.87}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60.01}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60.67}^{∘}"] ["math" "{68.12}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40561" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{68.12}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the acute angle between the vectors\n $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7} \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ \\text{ }4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}\\cdot (-\\sqrt{7})+7\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 7+2\\cdot 4}{\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{7})^{2}+{7}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{7})^{2}+{3}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\sqrt{64}\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" 