d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-5)+(-4)\\cdot (-5)+5\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-5)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{67}\\sqrt{55}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3685}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3685}})≈{70.76}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-40566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{70.76}^{∘}"] ["math" "{72.25}^{∘}"] ["math" "{75.5}^{∘}"] ["math" "{82.34}^{∘}"] ["math" "{89.76}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{70.76}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A(1,1,-1,-1)$, $B(2,4,6,8)$, and $C(1,2,3,4).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $v=\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $w=\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =b-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =c-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $\\theta =m∠BAC$ be the angle between the vectors $v$ and $w.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 4+9\\cdot 5}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{9}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{5}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{\\sqrt{140}\\cdot \\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{2\\sqrt{35}\\cdot \\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{14\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{7\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-140456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{19}{7\\sqrt{30}}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{30}}"] ["math" "\\frac{38}{7\\sqrt{30}}"] ["math" "\\frac{75}{14\\sqrt{30}}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{30}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{38}{7\\sqrt{30}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A(-1,3,2,-4)$, $B(1,0,1,-2)$, and $C(0,1,-1,2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $v=\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $w=\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =b-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =c-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $\\theta =m∠BAC$ be the angle between the vectors $v$ and $w.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{\\sqrt{18}\\cdot \\sqrt{50}} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-74121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{23}{30}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{23}{30}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{15}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{23}{30}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A(1,0,-1,2)$ and $B(4,8,2,-2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+0\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{88}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-140455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{22}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{22}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{132}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{22}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-140455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A(1,-1,2,0)$, $B(1,0,0,-1)$, and $C(0,1,1,0).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $v=\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $w=\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =b-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =c-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $\\theta =m∠BAC$ be the angle between the vectors $v$ and $w.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-40886" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40886" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13}{41}"] ["math" "\\frac{17}{\\sqrt{7}}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{87}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-40886" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A(1,-3,2,-1)$ and $B(1,1,3,-2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{15}\\cdot \\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{6÷3}{15÷3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b000fe912c3ae09c3ecb69305acdd03a23a9950894860b4685ecfac2076547b1"} {"question" "q-74105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "q-74105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/state.json" "file_sha256" "26564ba2655a02e5eddebf3be3b89a223a74e658e88b25b7d6044d31a6c34431"} {"question" "e-5554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/d1a095e61e6ea64f97a105fd69bc07f3f44990cd6d9794e54e355463c37a2413.png) Given that $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=-12$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v}\\Vert =4,$ what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/example-5554.json" "file_sha256" "10c2fdfd38d9aab8c868fa42ba8860e3cc9bbcdcbaa2467117aa742390226d41"} {"question" "e-5554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n\\vert \\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v} \\vert \\leq \\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert.$ So first, we compute $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-12| & \\le \\sqrt{6+k}\\cdot (4) \\\\ 12 & \\le 4\\sqrt{6+k} \\\\ 3 & \\le \\sqrt{6+k} \\\\ {3}^{2} & \\le (\\sqrt{6+k})^{2} \\\\ 9 & \\le 6+k \\\\ 3 & \\le k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/example-5554.json" "file_sha256" "10c2fdfd38d9aab8c868fa42ba8860e3cc9bbcdcbaa2467117aa742390226d41"} {"question" "e-5555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the acute angle between the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/5ed21f4bb536757026315cce838f4cc3028493adac2ff29d46a5b8cbdf11170b.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/8d813e104a708be37ba44b9448806f49ea21a16fe7f613314d2eeab2b59bbda2.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/example-5555.json" "file_sha256" "26639503442f1615eff0a22961b6e6afd46fee0533b14c4a5b3b6ee1d8cf91d7"} {"question" "e-5555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}}{\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert \\, \\Vert \\mathbf{w}\\Vert},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta=\\arccos \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right)=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/example-5555.json" "file_sha256" "26639503442f1615eff0a22961b6e6afd46fee0533b14c4a5b3b6ee1d8cf91d7"} {"question" "e-5910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A(-2, 4, -2, 2)$ and $B(4, 0, -1, -4).$ Find the cosine of the angle $\\angle{AOB},$ where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/example-5910.json" "file_sha256" "3461fcf7937467939e8745cf5e6c1105c591faefd01599102266186ff6a0c80b"} {"question" "e-5910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta = m\\angle{AOB}$ be the angle between the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}.$ Then, we can find $\\cos \\theta$ using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{28}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{33}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/example-5910.json" "file_sha256" "3461fcf7937467939e8745cf5e6c1105c591faefd01599102266186ff6a0c80b"}] "usage" {"e-5910" [] "e-5554" [] "q-40886" [] "e-5555" [] "q-40559" []} "basis" 1701 "retractions" [[17592186134220 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFind the acute angle between the vectors $v = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $w = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186134253 :question/problem "Let $A(1,-1, 2, 0)$, $B(1, 0, 0,-1)$, and $C(0, 1, 1, 0)$. Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC$."] [17592186133503 :question/problem "Consider the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{k} \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ Given that $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=-12$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v}\\Vert =4$, what is the smallest possible value of $k$?"] [17592186133503 :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n\\vert \\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v} \\vert \\leq \\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$. So first, we compute $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖u‖ &= \\sqrt{1^{2} + (\\sqrt{k})^{2} + (-2)^{2} + 1^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{6 + k}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\mid u \\cdot v \\mid \\mid \\le ‖u‖ \\cdot ‖v‖; \\mid - 12 \\mid \\mid \\le \\sqrt{6 + k} \\cdot (4); 12\\begin{vmatrix}\\le 4\\sqrt{6 + k} \\\\ 3\\end{vmatrix}\\le \\sqrt{6 + k}; 3^{2}\\begin{vmatrix}\\le (\\sqrt{6 + k})^{2} \\\\ 9\\end{vmatrix}\\le 6 + k; 3 \\mid \\le k\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $3$."] [17592186133504 :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vectors $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186133504 :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}}{\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert \\, \\Vert \\mathbf{w}\\Vert}\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos θ &= \\frac{v_{1}w_{1} + v_{2}w_{2} + v_{3}w_{3} + v_{4}w_{4}}{\\sqrt{v_{1}^{2} + v_{2}^{2} + v_{3}^{2} + v_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{w_{1}^{2} + w_{2}^{2} + w_{3}^{2} + w_{4}^{2}}} \\\\\n&= ((-1) \\cdot (-2) + 2 \\cdot 2 + (-4) \\cdot (-2) + (-2) \\cdot 2)/(\\sqrt{(-1)^{2} + 2^{2} + (-4)^{2} + (-2)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + 2^{2} + (-2)^{2} + 2^{2}}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{25} \\cdot \\sqrt{16}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{10}{5 \\cdot 4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta=\\arccos \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2} \\right)=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$"] [17592186133554 :question/problem "Let $A(-2, 4, -2, 2)$ and $B(4, 0, -1, -4)$. Find the cosine of the angle $\\angle{AOB}$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin."] [17592186133554 :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\na = OA^(→) = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}, b = OB^(→) = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAlso, let\n\n$$\n\\theta = m\\angle{AOB}\n$$\n\nbe the angle between the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$. Then, we can find $\\cos \\theta$ using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos θ &= \\frac{a \\cdot b}{‖a‖‖b‖} \\\\\n&= \\frac{a_{1}b_{1} + a_{2}b_{2} + a_{3}b_{3} + a_{4}b_{4}}{\\sqrt{a_{1}^{2} + a_{2}^{2} + a_{3}^{2} + a_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{b_{1}^{2} + b_{2}^{2} + b_{3}^{2} + b_{4}^{2}}} \\\\\n&= ((-2) \\cdot 4 + 4 \\cdot 0 + (-2) \\cdot (-1) + 2 \\cdot (-4))/(\\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + 4^{2} + (-2)^{2} + 2^{2}}\\sqrt{4^{2} + 0^{2} + (-1)^{2} + (-4)^{2}})) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{28} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{14} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\\n&=-\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{33}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186131763 17592186131764 17592186131765 17592186131766 17592186131767 17592186131961 17592186131962 17592186131963 17592186131964 17592186131965] "immutable_fields" [[17592186131762 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131762 :answer-field/id] [17592186131762 :answer-field/key] [17592186131762 :answer-field/type] [17592186131960 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131960 :answer-field/id] [17592186131960 :answer-field/key] [17592186131960 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
